<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Reading the amplitude, period, midline, maximum and minimum from a graph</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The graph below shows a wave-shaped curve. It repeats the same shape over and over, just like the graphs of \(y = \sin x\) and \(y = \cos x\).</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Graph of a repeating wave-shaped curve for x from 0 to 2 pi.">
[[jsxgraph width="600px" height="380px"]]
(function() {
  var A = {#A#}, B = {#B#}, D = {#D#};
  var top = A + D + 1.2, bot = D - A - 1;
  if (top < 1) { top = 1; } if (bot > -1) { bot = -1; }
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-0.8, top, 2*Math.PI + 1.6, bot], axis:false, grid:false,
      keepaspectratio:false, showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false});
  function gcd(m, n) { return n === 0 ? m : gcd(n, m % n); }
  function lab(k, n) {              /* label for k*pi/n */
    var g = gcd(k, n), p = k/g, q = n/g;
    var t = (p === 1 ? '' : p) + 'π';
    return q === 1 ? t : t + '/' + q;
  }
  var nt = 2*B, step = Math.PI/nt;  /* gridlines every quarter of a period */
  for (var k = 1; k <= 2*nt; k++) {
    var x0 = k*step;
    b.create('segment', [[x0, bot + 0.3], [x0, top - 0.3]], {strokeColor:'#eceff1', strokeWidth:1, fixed:true, highlight:false});
    b.create('segment', [[x0, -0.08], [x0, 0.08]], {strokeColor:'#444', fixed:true});
    if (k % 2 === 0 || B === 1) {
      b.create('text', [x0, -0.15, lab(k, nt)], {fixed:true, anchorX:'middle', anchorY:'top', fontSize:11});
    }
  }
  for (var j = Math.ceil(bot + 0.3); j <= Math.floor(top - 0.3); j++) {
    if (j !== 0) {
      b.create('segment', [[0, j], [2*Math.PI, j]], {strokeColor:'#eceff1', strokeWidth:1, fixed:true, highlight:false});
      b.create('segment', [[-0.06, j], [0.06, j]], {strokeColor:'#444', fixed:true});
      b.create('text', [-0.12, j, '' + j], {fixed:true, anchorX:'right', anchorY:'middle', fontSize:11});
    }
  }
  b.create('arrow', [[-0.4, 0], [2*Math.PI + 0.5, 0]], {strokeColor:'#444', fixed:true, highlight:false});
  b.create('arrow', [[0, bot + 0.1], [0, top - 0.05]], {strokeColor:'#444', fixed:true, highlight:false});
  b.create('text', [2*Math.PI + 0.45, -0.2, 'x'], {fixed:true}); b.create('text', [0.08, top - 0.25, 'y'], {fixed:true});
  b.create('functiongraph', [function(t) { return A*Math.cos(B*t) + D; }, 0, 2*Math.PI], {strokeColor:'#1565c0', strokeWidth:3, fixed:true});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>
<p><i>Use the graph to answer the questions below. Type \(\pi\) as <code>pi</code></i></p>

<p><strong>(a)</strong> Write down the <strong>maximum</strong> value and the <strong>minimum</strong> value.</p>
<div>Maximum value: [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>
<div>Minimum value: [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]</div>

<p><strong>(b)</strong> The <strong>midline</strong> is the horizontal line halfway between the highest and lowest points of the curve. Find its equation. </p>
<div>Midline: \(y = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>

<p><strong>(c)</strong> Find the <strong>amplitude</strong> of the curve. </p>
<div>Amplitude: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><strong>(d)</strong> Find the <strong>period</strong> of the curve, the horizontal length of one complete wave. </p>
<div>Period: [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<h4>(a) Maximum and minimum</h4>
<p><strong>Step 1: read the highest and lowest points.</strong> The highest points of the curve are at \(y = {@ta_max@}\) and the lowest points are at \(y = {@ta_min@}\).</p>
<p>Maximum value \(= {@ta_max@}\), minimum value \(= {@ta_min@}\).</p>

<h4>(b) Midline</h4>
<p><strong>Step 2: find the value halfway between them.</strong> Add the maximum and minimum, then halve:</p>
\[ y = \frac{\text{max} + \text{min}}{2} = \frac{ {@ta_max@} + ({@ta_min@}) }{2} = {@ta_midline@}. \]
<p>The midline is \(y = {@ta_midline@}\).</p>

<h4>(c) Amplitude</h4>
<p><strong>Step 3: find the height from the midline to the top.</strong> This is half of the maximum minus the minimum:</p>
\[ \text{amplitude} = \frac{\text{max} - \text{min}}{2} = \frac{ {@ta_max@} - ({@ta_min@}) }{2} = {@ta_amp@}. \]
<p>You can check it: from the midline \(y = {@ta_midline@}\) up to the maximum \(y = {@ta_max@}\) is \({@ta_amp@}\) units.</p>

<h4>(d) Period</h4>
<p><strong>Step 4: measure one complete wave.</strong> The curve has a maximum at \(x = 0\), and the next maximum is at \(x = {@xmax2@}\). So one complete wave has length</p>
\[ \text{period} = {@xmax2@} - 0 = {@ta_period@}. \]
<p>[[if test="is(B>1)"]]Check: there are \({@B@}\) complete waves between \(0\) and \(2\pi\), so each one has length \(\dfrac{2\pi}{ {@B@} } = {@ta_period@}\).[[else]]Check: there is exactly one complete wave between \(0\) and \(2\pi\), so the period is \(2\pi\).[[/if]]</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Graph of a repeating wave-shaped curve for x from 0 to 2 pi.">
[[jsxgraph width="600px" height="380px"]]
(function() {
  var A = {#A#}, B = {#B#}, D = {#D#};
  var top = A + D + 1.2, bot = D - A - 1;
  if (top < 1) { top = 1; } if (bot > -1) { bot = -1; }
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-0.8, top, 2*Math.PI + 1.6, bot], axis:false, grid:false,
      keepaspectratio:false, showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false});
  function gcd(m, n) { return n === 0 ? m : gcd(n, m % n); }
  function lab(k, n) {              /* label for k*pi/n */
    var g = gcd(k, n), p = k/g, q = n/g;
    var t = (p === 1 ? '' : p) + 'π';
    return q === 1 ? t : t + '/' + q;
  }
  var nt = 2*B, step = Math.PI/nt;  /* gridlines every quarter of a period */
  for (var k = 1; k <= 2*nt; k++) {
    var x0 = k*step;
    b.create('segment', [[x0, bot + 0.3], [x0, top - 0.3]], {strokeColor:'#eceff1', strokeWidth:1, fixed:true, highlight:false});
    b.create('segment', [[x0, -0.08], [x0, 0.08]], {strokeColor:'#444', fixed:true});
    if (k % 2 === 0 || B === 1) {
      b.create('text', [x0, -0.15, lab(k, nt)], {fixed:true, anchorX:'middle', anchorY:'top', fontSize:11});
    }
  }
  for (var j = Math.ceil(bot + 0.3); j <= Math.floor(top - 0.3); j++) {
    if (j !== 0) {
      b.create('segment', [[0, j], [2*Math.PI, j]], {strokeColor:'#eceff1', strokeWidth:1, fixed:true, highlight:false});
      b.create('segment', [[-0.06, j], [0.06, j]], {strokeColor:'#444', fixed:true});
      b.create('text', [-0.12, j, '' + j], {fixed:true, anchorX:'right', anchorY:'middle', fontSize:11});
    }
  }
  b.create('arrow', [[-0.4, 0], [2*Math.PI + 0.5, 0]], {strokeColor:'#444', fixed:true, highlight:false});
  b.create('arrow', [[0, bot + 0.1], [0, top - 0.05]], {strokeColor:'#444', fixed:true, highlight:false});
  b.create('text', [2*Math.PI + 0.45, -0.2, 'x'], {fixed:true}); b.create('text', [0.08, top - 0.25, 'y'], {fixed:true});
  b.create('functiongraph', [function(t) { return A*Math.cos(B*t) + D; }, 0, 2*Math.PI], {strokeColor:'#1565c0', strokeWidth:3, fixed:true});
  b.create('segment', [[0, A + D], [2*Math.PI, A + D]], {strokeColor:'#2e7d32', dash:2, fixed:true});
  b.create('segment', [[0, D - A], [2*Math.PI, D - A]], {strokeColor:'#2e7d32', dash:2, fixed:true});
  b.create('segment', [[0, D], [2*Math.PI, D]], {strokeColor:'#6a1b9a', dash:3, strokeWidth:2, fixed:true});
  b.create('text', [2*Math.PI + 0.1, A + D, 'max ' + (A + D)], {fixed:true, color:'#2e7d32', fontSize:11, anchorY:'middle'});
  b.create('text', [2*Math.PI + 0.1, D - A, 'min ' + (D - A)], {fixed:true, color:'#2e7d32', fontSize:11, anchorY:'middle'});
  b.create('text', [2*Math.PI + 0.1, D, 'midline y = ' + D], {fixed:true, color:'#6a1b9a', fontSize:11, anchorY:'middle'});
  var p = 2*Math.PI/B, yb = A + D + 0.45;
  b.create('point', [0, A + D], {name:'', size:4, color:'#c62828', fixed:true});
  b.create('point', [p, A + D], {name:'', size:4, color:'#c62828', fixed:true});
  b.create('arrow', [[p/2, yb], [0, yb]], {strokeColor:'#c62828', fixed:true});
  b.create('arrow', [[p/2, yb], [p, yb]], {strokeColor:'#c62828', fixed:true});
  b.create('text', [p/2, yb + 0.1, 'one period'], {fixed:true, color:'#c62828', anchorX:'middle', anchorY:'bottom', fontSize:11});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>
<p><strong>Final answers:</strong> maximum \({@ta_max@}\), minimum \({@ta_min@}\), midline \(y = {@ta_midline@}\), amplitude \({@ta_amp@}\), period \({@ta_period@}\). (The curve is \(y = {@f@}\).)</p>]]></text>
